# super-remap turns the physical left Super (keycode 133) into the F13 keysym,
# so it isn't a modifier and Gdk never sets MOD4 when it's held. The daemon
# uses libX11 directly for two jobs that Gdk doesn't expose cleanly:
#   - XQueryKeymap to read whether keycode 133 is currently held when the
#     popup opens (bootstraps the super_held flag for the first chord).
#   - XGrabKey + XNextEvent in a background thread to own the F13 launch
#     binding ourselves; mutter's custom-keybinding flow holds an active
#     keyboard grab from press until release, which blocks the popup's own
#     seat grab while Super is still down. Owning the grab lets us use
#     GrabModeAsync so events flow freely.
